{"id":"fujifilm_reala_ace","name":"Fujifilm Reala Ace","manufacturer":"Fujifilm","kind":"Negative","isBlackAndWhite":false,"source":"Negs","targetPrint":"fujifilm_crystal_archive_typeii","datasheet":{"url":"https://asset.fujifilm.com/www/jp/files/2024-04/2dca996da7fa6b3e34edda4c943870c2/datasheet_realaace_01.pdf","title":"Fujicolor Reala Ace data sheet (Japanese)"},"credit":"Copyright (c) 2026 Noah Haasis (Negs preparation). Method and generic dye spectra by Andrea Volpato (spektrafilm). Measurement data (c) FUJIFILM Corporation.","license":"Negs film profile, licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). Prepared with the profile-creation method of spektrafilm by Andrea Volpato (https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm; profiles CC BY-SA 4.0, see SPEKTRAFILM_LICENSE.txt) and its generic dye spectra. Derivatives must credit both, note their modifications and remain CC BY-SA 4.0. Changes: data/CHANGELOG.txt.","dataSource":"Prepared for Negs from the manufacturer's datasheet: FUJICOLOR REALA ACE data sheet (Japanese), Ref. No. 013Ai158A, 1996 (layout stamp 96.3-HB), PDF page 4 (spectral sensitivity, characteristic curves, minimum and midscale-neutral spectral density; RMS granularity 4). PDF sha256 04bb3116657b2263aa19682ff56cb41c779ed14931272325d42e9f753b64b918. Data (c) FUJIFILM Corporation. The curves were read from the PDF's vector paths (tools/film_profiles/extract_pdf.py); the points and axis calibration are in data/profile-sources/fujifilm-jp/fujifilm_reala_ace/.\nMethod: spektrafilm's public-era profile creator by Andrea Volpato (commit b2c7fe6), steps 1-8: D-min removed, log E zero where green is 0.2 over D-min plus 3 stops, dye spectra reconstructed (dmid_dmin) from spektrafilm's generic_a dye set (Giorgianni, Madden & Kriss 2009, p. 112, via spektrafilm) because the datasheet gives no per-dye spectra, status-M unmixing, a 3 norm_cdfs curve fit, sensitivity balance, midscale alignment 'green' (of none/green/mid, the lowest grey-ramp neutrality error, none 0.088, green 0.076, mid 0.078, among those whose fujifilm_crystal_archive_typeii neutral filters fall in the shipped films' range), densitometer normalisation. Then Negs's steps: sensitivity scaled so an 18.4 % grey gives raw exposure 1 per channel under the reference illuminant, and spektrafilm's grey-ramp refinement run on spektrafilm 28bf883 through fujifilm_crystal_archive_typeii at data_trustability 0.3. hanatos2025 adaptation window [397.8, 21.8, 616.5, 61.3] fitted on the reflectance corpus (Otsu (https://github.com/enneract/otsu2018), Munsell (https://zenodo.org/records/3269912), human skin (https://www.nist.gov/programs-projects/reflectance-measurements-human-skin), forest colors (https://zenodo.org/records/3269920)) with a weak prior toward the median of spektrafilm's stored windows. Tools and procedure: tools/film_profiles, docs/adding-film-stocks.md.\nNegs choices: reference illuminant D55 (daylight stock, exposed at 5400 K); viewing illuminant D50; target print fujifilm_crystal_archive_typeii; log_sensitivity_density_over_min 1.0 as printed; spectra left empty (null) outside the published wavelength range; characteristic curves in log10 H as printed; use 'still' and antihalation 'weak' as the shipped Fujifilm still negatives (C200, X-TRA 400, Superia 200, Reala 100, Pro 160NS).\nNote: the datasheet's dashed fourth colour layer (第4の感色層, cyan-sensitive) is not modelled: the three-layer model takes the blue, green and red sensitive layers only\nRecorded validation exception: the reconstructed dyes reproduce D-mid minus D-min within 0.043 D (worst at 585 nm), over the 0.03 D criterion; the §D3 fallback (a flat extension past 700 nm) was not tried, as the worst point is not near 700 nm. Weighted per fujifilm_crystal_archive_typeii print channel the residual is R/G/B +0.0016, +0.0039, +0.0085 D, within the 0.01 D the method accepts for this case (approved by Noah 2026-11-14).\nRelative axes: sensitivity y axis: Relative sensitivity (log), no tick values: a 1.0 scale bar spans the two gridlines (one log unit). The offset is arbitrary; D5 rescales every channel so it does not reach the profile.\nRecorded extraction exceptions: characteristic y axis, gate 0.3 % of span: hand-drafted grid reused across Fujifilm Japan's data sheets (Venus 800 and Natura 1600 share the dye chart's residuals to 0.001 %): no straight axis reproduces the gridlines within 0.2 % (worst 0.23 %, 0.009 D). The extraction error is bounded by that residual whether the curves were drawn to the true scale or to the drawn grid. Physical check: Natura 1600 from these sheets against the independent Professional Film Data Guide AF3-207U trace of the same emulsion (Superia 1600): curves within 0.009 D, spectra within 0.021 D (README, calibration/natura_1600_vs_pfdg_superia_1600_curves.json, calibration/vs_pfdg_all_panels.json).","referenceIlluminant":"D55","densitometer":"status_M","densityMinimum":[0.222,0.607,0.8],"wavelengths":[380,385,390,395,400,405,410,415,420,425,430,435,440,445,450,455,460,465,470,475,480,485,490,495,500,505,510,515,520,525,530,535,540,545,550,555,560,565,570,575,580,585,590,595,600,605,610,615,620,625,630,635,640,645,650,655,660,665,670,675,680,685,690,695,700,705,710,715,720,725,730,735,740,745,750,755,760,765,770,775,780],"logSensitivity":[[null,null,-1.7171],[null,null,-1.5269],[null,null,-1.2608],[null,null,-0.96858],[null,null,-0.78882],[null,null,-0.67873],[null,null,-0.62624],[null,null,-0.61433],[null,null,-0.61035],[null,null,-0.60752],[null,null,-0.60484],[null,null,-0.60154],[null,null,-0.59615],[null,null,-0.57429],[null,null,-0.49987],[null,null,-0.41756],[null,null,-0.3362],[null,null,-0.26081],[null,null,-0.201],[null,null,-0.22071],[null,null,-0.49216],[null,-1.656,-0.94269],[null,-1.3464,-1.4089],[null,-1.0812,-1.896],[null,-0.86363,null],[null,-0.74003,null],[null,-0.65213,null],[null,-0.57697,null],[null,-0.50759,null],[null,-0.44003,null],[null,-0.37022,null],[null,-0.30313,null]